# Every entry here is a deliberate design decision, not an accepted risk backlog.
# Remove the entry in the same PR that changes the decision.

# The ledger volume is encrypted (enforced by the plan tests); it uses the
# account's EBS default key because the module does not yet surface a CMK input
# for the control plane. The cache path has enable_kms; adding a control-plane
# key input is additive work, not a default this module should impose.
AVD-AWS-0027

# Runner and control-plane security groups allow unrestricted egress by design:
# jobs fetch from GitHub, registries, and package mirrors, and the control plane
# long-polls GitHub. Ingress is what the module restricts.
AVD-AWS-0104

# The created subnet is public on purpose: the opinionated default is a small
# deployment whose control plane reaches GitHub without a NAT gateway's monthly
# cost. Operators with private-subnet requirements adopt their own network via
# vpc_id/subnet_id.
AVD-AWS-0164

# VPC flow logs are a monitoring decision with per-GB cost, left to the
# operator. The module's monitoring surface is deliberately left to the operator.
AVD-AWS-0178

# The cache bucket holds rebuildable build artifacts: access logging (AVD-AWS-0089)
# and versioning (AVD-AWS-0090) would multiply storage cost to protect data whose
# loss costs one cache rebuild.
#
# THE BACKUP BUCKET IS THE OPPOSITE CASE AND ANSWERS BOTH SEPARATELY, said here
# because these ids are module-wide and a reader would otherwise take the
# sentence above as covering it. It holds two private keys and a ledger, so it
# IS versioned (backup.tf enables it deliberately: versioning is what makes
# billet's never-delete credential mean something). What it does not have is
# ACCESS LOGGING, which needs a second bucket this child does not own and would
# have to create, name and lifecycle — an operator who needs to know who read
# their archives adds aws_s3_bucket_logging against a target of their choosing,
# and CloudTrail data events are the other answer. That is a decision left with
# them rather than a cost imposed by default.
AVD-AWS-0089
AVD-AWS-0090

# The cache bucket is SSE-S3 by default; enable_kms switches it to a
# customer-managed key with per-deployment read isolation. The default is
# deliberate: SSE-S3 has no key-management burden and the data is a build cache.
AVD-AWS-0132

# The spot-router Lambda is a hundred-line forwarder whose only work is moving an
# interruption warning onto the queue. X-Ray tracing (AVD-AWS-0066) would add a
# per-invocation cost to observe a function whose failures already land on one
# metric: the router re-raises rather than dropping anything it cannot prove is
# another deployment's, so a lost warning is an Errors datapoint, and
# aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.spot_router_errors watches exactly that. What is
# declined here is the TRACING, not the signal — and the alarm SENDS nothing
# until spot_router_alarm_actions names somewhere to send it, because this module
# creates no SNS topic and will not invent an alerting path an operator already
# has. A CMK on its log group (AVD-AWS-0017) is the same key-management burden
# the ledger entry above declines — the logs carry instance ids, not secrets.
AVD-AWS-0066
AVD-AWS-0017
